 <!-- next-header -->
 ## [Unreleased] - ReleaseDate
 
+### Fixes
+
+- `Arg::allow_negative_numbers` now accepts scientific notation with a signed exponent, like `-1e-5` and `-1E+3`
+- `ValueRange::new` now panics in debug builds on the empty ranges `0..0` and `..0`, as it already documented and already did for `5..5`
+- `Command::get_arg_conflicts_with` now reports a conflict from both sides, matching the parser, so a generated zsh completion no longer offers a flag combination the command refuses
+- Help text containing a tab, carriage return or other control character is measured correctly again; previously everything after the first such character counted as zero width, so the help overflowed `Command::term_width`
+- `clap_complete`: `Shell::Fish::try_generate` now returns a write failure instead of panicking when the command has subcommands, matching the other four shells
+- The usage line now wraps to `Command::term_width` like the rest of the help does, with its continuations aligned under the first line; a usage set with `Command::override_usage` across several lines keeps its own alignment
+- `Arg::hide_short_help` and `Arg::hide_long_help` are no longer overridden by `Arg::next_line_help` or `Command::next_line_help`; an argument setting both was previously shown on the route its hide flag named
+- A typo that differs only in case, like `--FLAG` for `--flag`, now draws a suggestion; the similarity score is 0 for such a pair, so nothing was offered at all. Flags, subcommands and values all use the one scorer, and the case-insensitive pass runs only when the case-sensitive one found nothing, so an input that already drew a suggestion draws the same one
+- `ArgGroup::is_multiple` takes `&self` rather than `&mut self`, like every other `ArgGroup` accessor, so asking a read-only question no longer needs a mutable binding
+- `BoolishValueParser` reports a rejected value as `ErrorKind::InvalidValue` and names every literal it accepts, matching `BoolValueParser`; it previously reported `ErrorKind::ValueValidation` with the message "value was not a boolean", which named none of them
+
